WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.973 --> 00:00:12.897
The kids rushed down the hill to Mango.

2
00:00:14.497 --> 00:00:16.518
He was lying in a crumpled heap.

3
00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:18.699
"Are you okay?"

4
00:00:19.179 --> 00:00:19.879
Ezra asked.

5
00:00:19.899 --> 00:00:22.701
"I twisted my ankle."

6
00:00:23.821 --> 00:00:25.161
Mango tried to stand up.

7
00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:27.122
"Owie, owie!"

8
00:00:27.142 --> 00:00:30.063
"Can you walk on it at all?"

9
00:00:30.524 --> 00:00:31.164
Ivy asked.

10
00:00:32.372 --> 00:00:33.572
Mango rubbed his ankle.

11
00:00:33.592 --> 00:00:35.873
"Owie, owie."

12
00:00:35.893 --> 00:00:38.914
"This is all your fault!"

13
00:00:39.314 --> 00:00:40.314
Huck yelled at Buck.

14
00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:42.575
"You pushed me into Mango."

15
00:00:42.595 --> 00:00:45.896
"It's your fault for being so clumsy!"

16
00:00:46.256 --> 00:00:47.156
Buck yelled back.

17
00:00:48.657 --> 00:00:50.977
Ivy rolled her eyes as the Ucks kept fighting.

18
00:00:50.997 --> 00:00:56.059
"Mango, what should we do to help you?"

19
00:00:56.599 --> 00:00:57.279
Ezra asked.

20
00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.580
Mango opened his mouth.

21
00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.382
The kids leaned forward, waiting for instructions.

22
00:01:03.402 --> 00:01:05.844
"Owie, owie!"

23
00:01:06.244 --> 00:01:07.525
was all Mango could say.

24
00:01:07.545 --> 00:01:10.287
"What are we going to do?"

25
00:01:10.888 --> 00:01:12.049
Ezra sounded panicked.

26
00:01:12.669 --> 00:01:14.070
"Mango can't walk.

27
00:01:15.231 --> 00:01:18.734
And it's against camp rules for campers to hike without a counselor."

28
00:01:19.975 --> 00:01:21.316
He looked around at the woods.

29
00:01:21.336 --> 00:01:23.758
"We're stuck here!

30
00:01:23.778 --> 00:01:26.700
We'll have to fight off bears!

31
00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:30.242
And eat tree bark to survive!"

32
00:01:36.986 --> 00:01:38.727
calm down," Glen said.

33
00:01:40.028 --> 00:01:42.590
To Ivy's surprise, everyone turned to him.

34
00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.412
"Ucks," Glen said.

35
00:01:45.432 --> 00:01:47.253
"Stop arguing.

36
00:01:47.794 --> 00:01:49.655
You're big enough to help Mango walk."

37
00:01:53.258 --> 00:01:55.559
"Hey! Who put you in charge?"

38
00:01:55.939 --> 00:01:56.520
Chuck said.

39
00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.421
"I did," Mango said.

40
00:01:59.441 --> 00:02:02.022
"Somebody has to take over for me.

41
00:02:02.542 --> 00:02:09.425
Owie!" Buck and Huck got on either side of Mango.

42
00:02:10.305 --> 00:02:12.166
He swung his arms over their shoulders.

43
00:02:12.826 --> 00:02:14.407
They all took slow steps.

44
00:02:15.547 --> 00:02:17.308
Mango hopped along on one foot.

45
00:02:17.328 --> 00:02:21.870
"See—no reason to panic," Glen said.

46
00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.331
"Now we just walk back to camp.

47
00:02:25.531 --> 00:02:26.411
Come on, everyone.

48
00:02:26.852 --> 00:02:27.532
Follow me."

49
00:02:29.576 --> 00:02:32.477
All the campers got behind Glen and started walking.

50
00:02:34.258 --> 00:02:36.679
Ivy and Ezra exchanged astonished looks.

51
00:02:37.499 --> 00:02:39.020
"What just happened?"

52
00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.220
Ezra asked.

53
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.162
"Since when does Glen actually know what to do?"

54
00:02:45.743 --> 00:02:46.583
Ivy shook her head.

55
00:02:46.603 --> 00:02:48.524
"I have no idea.

56
00:02:48.544 --> 00:02:50.124
Hey, Glen!"

57
00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:52.925
She caught up to him.

58
00:02:52.945 --> 00:02:57.027
"Wow! You took charge like a real leader."

59
00:02:57.047 --> 00:03:01.370
"Really? Me—a leader?"

60
00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:02.791
Glen chuckled.

61
00:03:02.811 --> 00:03:04.613
"I guess you're right."

62
00:03:06.054 --> 00:03:07.075
He stood up straighter.

63
00:03:07.095 --> 00:03:09.377
"I'm the leader of this group!"

64
00:03:10.137 --> 00:03:12.459
He threw his shoulders back and marched forward.

65
00:03:14.521 --> 00:03:15.262
Ezra moaned.

66
00:03:15.282 --> 00:03:18.645
"You shouldn't have said that, Ivy.

67
00:03:19.285 --> 00:03:20.746
You know how Glen gets.

68
00:03:22.087 --> 00:03:25.450
He'll brag about taking charge for the rest of the summer."

69
00:03:28.528 --> 00:03:29.569
"Oops." Ivy looked sheepish.

70
00:03:29.589 --> 00:03:31.551
"You're right, Ezra.

71
00:03:32.351 --> 00:03:34.453
I hope I haven't created a monster."

72
00:03:35.874 --> 00:03:36.635
Ezra sighed.

73
00:03:36.655 --> 00:03:38.597
"Me too.

74
00:03:39.477 --> 00:03:41.779
I'm the one who has to share a cabin with him."

75
00:03:44.321 --> 00:03:47.664
It took awhile, but the hikers finally arrived back at camp.

76
00:03:49.345 --> 00:03:51.627
When Private saw them, she rushed over.

77
00:03:51.647 --> 00:03:55.490
"We expected you back half an hour ago.

78
00:03:56.191 --> 00:03:57.012
What happened?"

79
00:03:58.428 --> 00:04:01.109
"I fell and twisted my ankle," Mango said.

80
00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:04.030
"We could have been stranded in the woods for hours.

81
00:04:04.591 --> 00:04:07.432
But He patted Glen's head.

82
00:04:07.452 --> 00:04:12.234
"But my little hero here organized everyone to get us back safely."

83
00:04:13.614 --> 00:04:15.755
Private looked at Glen and gave him a salute.

84
00:04:15.775 --> 00:04:18.296
"Congratulations, camper.

85
00:04:18.917 --> 00:04:22.978
It sounds like you seized control of a very dangerous situation."

86
00:04:22.998 --> 00:04:26.500
"Thanks." Glen frowned.

87
00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:30.702
"But I wouldn't call myself a little hero.

88
00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:35.726
What I did was pretty big—I'd call it huge, in fact!"

89
00:04:35.746 --> 00:04:39.128
"Uh-oh," Ivy thought.

90
00:04:39.148 --> 00:04:43.952
"There we were, surrounded by danger," Glen went on.

91
00:04:43.972 --> 00:04:47.994
"All of the less experienced hikers were panicking.

92
00:04:49.195 --> 00:04:52.597
Ezra was so hungry, he started eating tree bark!"

93
00:04:54.199 --> 00:04:56.020
"What?" Ezra squawked.

94
00:04:57.216 --> 00:04:58.057
Private frowned.

95
00:04:58.077 --> 00:05:01.179
"That's very bad for your teeth, camper.

96
00:05:01.779 --> 00:05:03.761
And it can't be good for the tree either."

97
00:05:03.781 --> 00:05:07.483
"No, I didn't!"

98
00:05:08.043 --> 00:05:08.624
Ezra said.

99
00:05:08.644 --> 00:05:14.328
"I—" "I knew I had to take charge, or we'd never survive!"

100
00:05:14.648 --> 00:05:15.288
Glen said.

101
00:05:15.308 --> 00:05:20.132
"I saved these campers from a fate worse than death!"
